From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/a733: kms: a cursor plane on VI channel 1 and blender pipe 1

The KMS device has exactly one plane, the primary. Every compositor
therefore draws the pointer into it and recomposites a full frame per
pointer event; on the desktop image that is labwc through zink on the GPU. This adds a DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR plane that the
display engine blends in hardware.

WHERE IT LIVES

VI channel slot 1, blender port 1, blender pipe 1 above pipe 0. VI rather
than UI because the VI layer block is the one witnessed on silicon (slot 0,
sun60i-de.c); a UI channel's layer layout is witnessed nowhere. Pipe = port
= 1, and the vendor's own live map has VI1 on port 1 (de_top +0x30 =
0x0000a810 on its link: port 0 VI0, port 1 VI1, port 2 UI0, port 3 UI2).

THE WORD THAT WAS MISSING

de_top +0x30, PORT2CHN_MUX (allwinner-bsp lowlevel_de/de_top.c, the V2
offset the de352 descriptor selects; de_top_set_port2chn_mux()): 4 bits per
blender port, VI 0..7, UI id + 8. Its reset value 0 names VI0 on every
port, which serves the primary and nothing else. Measured by raw register
stimulus before this patch:
slot 1 and pipe 1 fully programmed, every word reading back, and the sink's
frame CRC does not move; the same pipe enable with PORT2CHN = 0x10 toggles
the CRC between two stable values twice, and a COORD write alone moves it.
sun60i_de_top_setup() now writes port 0 = VI0, port 1 = VI1 on every
start.

THE LAYER WORD

ATTCTL from the vendor's field map (lowlevel_de/ovl/de_ovl_type.h,
ovl_v_attctl_reg) and its composition for a layer whose alpha is used
(de_ovl.c, the lay[i].ctl word): alpha mode 2 = pixel alpha times global
alpha 0xff, FBFMT 0 = ARGB8888 (MSB A-R-G-B LSB, DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888),
RGB_MODE, PREMUL [17:16] = 2 "has premul". The blender gets
BLD_PREMULTIPLY bit 1 for pipe 1, as de_bld_set_premul() does for a
premultiplied channel. Premultiplied is DRM's default blend mode for a
plane without the property, and what cursor clients hand in.

WHAT THE VENDOR DOES DIFFERENTLY

  - It registers no cursor plane at all: drm_crtc_init_with_planes() gets
    NULL for the cursor (sunxi_drm_crtc.c:2513) and every other channel
    becomes an OVERLAY plane. The legacy cursor ioctl and a compositor's
    cursor-plane path find nothing there either; here both land on pipe 1.
  - It chooses ports through a per-mode channel table and rewrites the whole
    port map per commit; here the map is fixed, because two channels are
    all this driver drives.
  - Its plane update writes crtc_x/y straight into the 16-bit coordinate
    field (de_bld.c:246-250), so a pointer at the left or top edge becomes
    a coordinate near 65535. Here drm_atomic_helper_check_plane_state()
    clips, and the clipped source origin goes into the layer address, the
    same path the primary already takes.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO

  - One format, ARGB8888. XRGB8888 would be a different ATTCTL, and an
    opaque square is not a cursor.
  - No line-window guard, like every other write in this driver: a move
    lands mid-frame, so for one frame the cursor can be split between two
    heights. Because the writes take effect as they are made, slot 1 stops
    reading the previous buffer once the update returns, which is what the
    legacy cursor path's skipped vblank wait relies on.
  - cursor_width/height = 64 is the size hint userspace reads through
    DRM_CAP_CURSOR_WIDTH; the layer itself takes any size the primary does.

The cursor is switched off before the primary on the way down
(sun60i_de_stop()): slot 1 is a bus master reading a buffer the DRM core
may free once the commit returns. A modeset starts the DE from reset, where
slot 1 and pipe 1 are off; the cursor's atomic_update in the same commit
turns it back on.

FALSIFIERS

  1. drm_info lists a second plane on the CRTC, type Cursor, format AR24;
     DRM_CAP_CURSOR_WIDTH reads 64.
  2. A cursor committed at (x, y) changes the sink CRC; the same commit
     without the cursor restores the previous value; debugfs `state` shows
     PORT2CHN_MUX0 0x10, vi1 LAY0_ATTCTL 0xff028005, bld0 PREMULTIPLY 0x2,
     COORD1 = (y << 16) | x.
  3. A cursor half off the left edge shows its right half at x = 0 (the
     clipped source offset), not a wrapped coordinate.
  4. Before/after under labwc with the pointer moving: flips per second and
     labwc CPU; after, no full-frame composite per pointer event.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff -u a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c
@@ -184,6 +184,17 @@
 #define   DE_TOP_ENABLE2_VALUE		0x00000011
 #define  DE_TOP_DE2TCON_MUX		0x0010
 #define  DE_TOP_VERSION			0x0014
+/*
+ * Which channel feeds which blender port: one word per display, 4 bits per
+ * port, VI channels 0..7, UI channels id + 8. The name and the V2 offset are
+ * the vendor's (allwinner-bsp lowlevel_de/de_top.c, DE_PORT2CHN_MUX_OFFSET_V2,
+ * selected by the de352 descriptor; de_top_set_port2chn_mux()). Reset is 0,
+ * which names VI0 on every port -- enough for the primary on port 0, and the
+ * reason a second channel on pipe 1 showed nothing until port 1 was pointed
+ * at VI1.
+ */
+#define  DE_TOP_PORT2CHN_MUX0		0x0030
+#define   PORT2CHN_PORT(p, chn)		((chn) << (4 * (p)))
 
 #define DE_MIXER0_TOP			0x008100
 #define  MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL		0x0000
@@ -219,6 +230,17 @@
 #define DE_VI0_SLOT			0
 #define DE_BLD_PIPE			0
 
+/*
+ * The cursor: VI slot 1 on blender port 1, blended by pipe 1 above pipe 0.
+ * VI and not UI because the VI layer layout is the one witnessed on silicon
+ * (slot 0 above); a UI channel's layer block is witnessed nowhere. Port 1 is
+ * the port the vendor's own live map gives VI1 (de_top +0x30 = 0xa810 on its
+ * link: port 0 VI0, port 1 VI1). Pipe = port = 1 keeps the route readable.
+ */
+#define DE_CURSOR_SLOT			1
+#define DE_CURSOR_PORT			1
+#define DE_CURSOR_PIPE			1
+
 /*
  * Four blender register files at a 0x400 stride, all four programmed
  * identically on the live link, on a board with exactly one display pipe up.
@@ -238,7 +260,9 @@
 #define  BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(p)		(0x0008 + 0x10 * (p))
 #define  BLD_ATTR_COORD(p)		(0x000c + 0x10 * (p))
 #define  BLD_ROUTE			0x0080
+#define   BLD_ROUTE_PIPE(p, port)	((port) << (4 * (p)))
 #define  BLD_PREMULTIPLY		0x0084
+#define   BLD_PREMULTIPLY_PIPE(p)	BIT(p)
 #define  BLD_BKCOLOR			0x0088
 #define  BLD_OUTSIZE			0x008c
 #define  BLD_MODE(p)			(0x0090 + 0x04 * (p))
@@ -247,6 +271,7 @@
 #define DE_OVL_LAYER			0
 #define  OVL_LAY_ATTCTL(l)		(0x30 * (l) + 0x0000)
 #define   OVL_ATTCTL_ALPHA		GENMASK(31, 24)
+#define   OVL_ATTCTL_PREMUL		GENMASK(17, 16)
 #define   OVL_ATTCTL_RGB_MODE		BIT(15)
 #define   OVL_ATTCTL_FBFMT		GENMASK(12, 8)
 #define   OVL_ATTCTL_ALPHA_MODE		GENMASK(2, 1)
@@ -331,8 +356,11 @@
 #define DE2TCON_MUX_LIVE		0x0000fff5
 #define BLD_COLOR_BLACK			0xff000000
 #define BLD_MODE_SRCOVER		0x03010301
+#define OVL_FBFMT_ARGB8888		0
 #define OVL_FBFMT_XRGB8888		4
 #define OVL_ALPHA_MODE_LAYER		1
+#define OVL_ALPHA_MODE_COMBINED		2
+#define OVL_PREMUL_HAS_PREMUL		2
 #define DE_ALPHA_OPAQUE			0xff
 #define DE_BYTES_PER_PIXEL		4
 
@@ -425,6 +453,7 @@ struct sun60i_de {
 	const struct sun60i_de_commit	*commit;
 	bool				enabled;
 	bool				layer_on;
+	bool				cursor_on;
 	bool				ccsc_on;
 	/*
 	 * A KMS master is bound and owns the datapath. The debugfs verbs that
@@ -883,6 +912,9 @@ static void sun60i_de_top_setup(struct sun60i_de *de)
 	u32 size = DE_SIZE(mode->hdisplay, mode->vdisplay);
 
 	sun60i_de_write(de, DE_TOP + DE_TOP_DE2TCON_MUX, DE2TCON_MUX_LIVE);
+	sun60i_de_write(de, DE_TOP + DE_TOP_PORT2CHN_MUX0,
+			PORT2CHN_PORT(DE_BLD_PIPE, DE_VI0_SLOT) |
+			PORT2CHN_PORT(DE_CURSOR_PORT, DE_CURSOR_SLOT));
 	sun60i_de_write(de, DE_MIXER0_TOP + MIXER_GLOBAL_SIZE, size);
 	sun60i_de_write(de, DE_MIXER0_TOP + MIXER_GLOBAL_CLK, 1);
 	sun60i_de_write(de, DE_MIXER0_TOP + MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL,
@@ -1204,6 +1236,107 @@ static int sun60i_de_layer_disable(struct sun60i_de *de)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The cursor layer: VI slot 1, one layer, ARGB8888 with the pixel's own alpha,
+ * premultiplied -- DRM's default blend mode, and what cursor clients hand in.
+ *
+ * ATTCTL is built from the vendor's field map and its own composition for a
+ * layer whose alpha is not ignored (allwinner-bsp lowlevel_de/ovl/de_ovl.c,
+ * the lay[i].ctl word; de_channel.c, de_rtmx_chn_blend_attr()):
+ *   ALPHA_MODE [2:1] = 2  pixel alpha times global alpha, global = 0xff
+ *   FBFMT     [12:8] = 0  ARGB8888, MSB A-R-G-B LSB = DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888
+ *   RGB_MODE     [15]     as for the primary
+ *   PREMUL   [17:16] = 2  the pixels are already premultiplied
+ * and the blender is told the same per pipe (BLD_PREMULTIPLY bit 1), which is
+ * what the vendor's de_bld_set_premul() does for a premultiplied channel.
+ *
+ * The high-address bytes (+0xd0..+0xe4) are not written: the DE comes out of
+ * reset with them at 0 on every slot, and nothing in this driver sets them
+ *.
+ *
+ * The blender words go to all four instances, like every other blender write
+ * in this file. PIPE_CTL is written whole, pipe 0's bits included, because
+ * the register holds both pipes and nothing else owns it.
+ */
+static u32 sun60i_de_cursor_attctl(void)
+{
+	return FIELD_PREP(OVL_ATTCTL_ALPHA, DE_ALPHA_OPAQUE) |
+	       FIELD_PREP(OVL_ATTCTL_PREMUL, OVL_PREMUL_HAS_PREMUL) |
+	       OVL_ATTCTL_RGB_MODE |
+	       FIELD_PREP(OVL_ATTCTL_FBFMT, OVL_FBFMT_ARGB8888) |
+	       FIELD_PREP(OVL_ATTCTL_ALPHA_MODE, OVL_ALPHA_MODE_COMBINED) |
+	       OVL_ATTCTL_EN;
+}
+
+static int sun60i_de_cursor_enable(struct sun60i_de *de,
+				   const struct drm_rect *dst,
+				   dma_addr_t addr, u32 pitch)
+{
+	u32 ovl = sun60i_de_chn(DE_CURSOR_SLOT) + DE_CHN_OVL;
+	u32 size = DE_SIZE(drm_rect_width(dst), drm_rect_height(dst));
+	u32 coord = DE_COORD(dst->x1, dst->y1);
+	unsigned int i;
+	int ret;
+
+	de->commit->begin(de);
+
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_LAY_MBSIZE(DE_OVL_LAYER), size);
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_LAY_MBCOOR(DE_OVL_LAYER), 0);
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_LAY_PITCH(DE_OVL_LAYER, 0), pitch);
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_LAY_TOP_LADDR(DE_OVL_LAYER, 0),
+			lower_32_bits(addr));
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_VI_OVL_SIZE, size);
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_LAY_ATTCTL(DE_OVL_LAYER),
+			sun60i_de_cursor_attctl());
+
+	for (i = 0; i < DE_BLD_INSTANCES; i++) {
+		u32 bld = sun60i_de_bld(i);
+
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(DE_CURSOR_PIPE), size);
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_COORD(DE_CURSOR_PIPE), coord);
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_MODE(DE_CURSOR_PIPE),
+				BLD_MODE_SRCOVER);
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ROUTE,
+				BLD_ROUTE_PIPE(DE_BLD_PIPE, 0) |
+				BLD_ROUTE_PIPE(DE_CURSOR_PIPE, DE_CURSOR_PORT));
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_PREMULTIPLY,
+				BLD_PREMULTIPLY_PIPE(DE_CURSOR_PIPE));
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_PIPE_CTL,
+				BLD_PIPE_CTL_EN(DE_BLD_PIPE) |
+				BLD_PIPE_CTL_FC_EN(DE_BLD_PIPE) |
+				BLD_PIPE_CTL_EN(DE_CURSOR_PIPE));
+	}
+
+	ret = de->commit->arm(de);
+	de->cursor_on = true;
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Pipe first, then the layer, so no frame blends a half-disabled channel. On
+ * the way down (sun60i_de_stop()) this runs before the quiesce, for the same
+ * reason the primary layer does: slot 1 is a bus master reading a buffer the
+ * DRM core may free as soon as the commit returns.
+ */
+static int sun60i_de_cursor_disable(struct sun60i_de *de)
+{
+	u32 ovl = sun60i_de_chn(DE_CURSOR_SLOT) + DE_CHN_OVL;
+	unsigned int i;
+	int ret;
+
+	de->commit->begin(de);
+	for (i = 0; i < DE_BLD_INSTANCES; i++)
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, sun60i_de_bld(i) + BLD_PIPE_CTL,
+				BLD_PIPE_CTL_EN(DE_BLD_PIPE) |
+				BLD_PIPE_CTL_FC_EN(DE_BLD_PIPE));
+	sun60i_de_stage(de, ovl + OVL_LAY_ATTCTL(DE_OVL_LAYER), 0);
+	ret = de->commit->arm(de);
+	de->cursor_on = false;
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /*
  * Stage the layer on or off through the commit path, and nothing else.
  *
@@ -1375,6 +1508,8 @@ static void sun60i_de_stop(struct sun60i_de *de)
 	 * refuses to stop leaves the block fetching from pages that are about
 	 * to belong to somebody else.
 	 */
+	if (de->cursor_on)
+		sun60i_de_cursor_disable(de);
 	sun60i_de_layer_disable(de);
 	sun60i_de_quiesce(de);
 	sun60i_de_clocks_off(de);
@@ -1433,6 +1568,16 @@ static int sun60i_de_state_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 		{ "bld0 BKCOLOR",	bld + BLD_BKCOLOR },
 		{ "bld0 OUTSIZE",	bld + BLD_OUTSIZE },
 		{ "bld0 BLEND_MODE0",	bld + BLD_MODE(DE_BLD_PIPE) },
+		{ "de_top PORT2CHN_MUX0", DE_TOP + DE_TOP_PORT2CHN_MUX0 },
+		{ "vi1 LAY0_ATTCTL (cursor)",
+		  sun60i_de_chn(DE_CURSOR_SLOT) + DE_CHN_OVL +
+		  OVL_LAY_ATTCTL(DE_OVL_LAYER) },
+		{ "vi1 LAY0_TOP_LADDR0 (cursor)",
+		  sun60i_de_chn(DE_CURSOR_SLOT) + DE_CHN_OVL +
+		  OVL_LAY_TOP_LADDR(DE_OVL_LAYER, 0) },
+		{ "bld0 INSIZE1 (cursor)", bld + BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(DE_CURSOR_PIPE) },
+		{ "bld0 COORD1 (cursor)", bld + BLD_ATTR_COORD(DE_CURSOR_PIPE) },
+		{ "bld0 PREMULTIPLY",	bld + BLD_PREMULTIPLY },
 	};
 	const struct sun60i_de_reg traps[] = {
 		{ "vi0 CCSC_CTL",		chn + DE_CHN_CCSC + CCSC_CTL },
@@ -1616,6 +1761,40 @@ void sun60i_de_kms_layer_off(struct sun60i_de *de)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sun60i_de_kms_layer_off);
 
+/*
+ * The cursor plane's two calls. Same commit path and the same missing
+ * line-window guard as sun60i_de_kms_scanout() -- a move lands mid-frame, so
+ * for one frame the cursor can sit at two heights. The writes take effect as
+ * they are made, so once this returns slot 1 no longer fetches the previous
+ * buffer, which is what the legacy cursor path's skipped vblank wait relies
+ * on.
+ */
+int sun60i_de_kms_cursor(struct sun60i_de *de, const struct drm_rect *dst,
+			 dma_addr_t addr, u32 pitch)
+{
+	guard(mutex)(&de->lock);
+
+	if (!de->enabled)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	if (!sun60i_de_dst_fits(&de->mode, dst))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	return sun60i_de_cursor_enable(de, dst, addr, pitch);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sun60i_de_kms_cursor);
+
+void sun60i_de_kms_cursor_off(struct sun60i_de *de)
+{
+	guard(mutex)(&de->lock);
+
+	if (!de->enabled || !de->cursor_on)
+		return;
+
+	sun60i_de_cursor_disable(de);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sun60i_de_kms_cursor_off);
+
 /*
  * The component hooks do no hardware work at all, and that is deliberate: this
  * driver is started by a modeset, not by a bind, exactly as it is started by a
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-kms.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-kms.c
@@ -529,6 +529,64 @@ static const struct drm_plane_helper_funcs sun60i_kms_plane_helper_funcs = {
 	.atomic_disable	= sun60i_kms_plane_atomic_disable,
 };
 
+/*
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * The cursor plane
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ *
+ * VI slot 1, blended by pipe 1 above the primary (sun60i-de.c, above
+ * sun60i_de_cursor_attctl()). Without it every compositor draws the pointer
+ * into the primary and recomposites a frame per pointer event.
+ *
+ * ARGB8888 only: the layer takes the pixel's alpha, premultiplied, which is
+ * DRM's default blend mode for a plane without a "pixel blend mode" property
+ * and what cursor clients hand in. XRGB8888 would need a different ATTCTL,
+ * and an opaque square is not what anyone wants as a cursor.
+ *
+ * The checks are the primary's, word for word (sun60i_kms_plane_atomic_check()):
+ * positioned but not scaled, whole-pixel source origin, a scanout address
+ * below 4 GiB. A cursor that hangs over an edge is clipped by the helper and
+ * its source offset goes into the address, as for the primary. What differs
+ * is that a cursor may be absent or wholly off the mode: both mean pipe 1 off.
+ */
+static const u32 sun60i_kms_cursor_formats[] = {
+	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
+};
+
+static void sun60i_kms_cursor_atomic_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
+					    struct drm_atomic_state *state)
+{
+	struct drm_plane_state *new_state =
+		drm_atomic_get_new_plane_state(state, plane);
+	struct sun60i_kms *kms = to_kms_plane(plane)->kms;
+	dma_addr_t addr;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!new_state->visible) {
+		sun60i_de_kms_cursor_off(kms->de);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	addr = sun60i_kms_plane_scanout(new_state);
+
+	ret = sun60i_de_kms_cursor(kms->de, &new_state->dst, addr,
+				   new_state->fb->pitches[0]);
+	if (ret)
+		drm_err(plane->dev, "cursor from %pad: %d\n", &addr, ret);
+}
+
+static void sun60i_kms_cursor_atomic_disable(struct drm_plane *plane,
+					     struct drm_atomic_state *state)
+{
+	sun60i_de_kms_cursor_off(to_kms_plane(plane)->kms->de);
+}
+
+static const struct drm_plane_helper_funcs sun60i_kms_cursor_helper_funcs = {
+	.atomic_check	= sun60i_kms_plane_atomic_check,
+	.atomic_update	= sun60i_kms_cursor_atomic_update,
+	.atomic_disable	= sun60i_kms_cursor_atomic_disable,
+};
+
 static const struct drm_plane_funcs sun60i_kms_plane_funcs = {
 	.update_plane		= drm_atomic_helper_update_plane,
 	.disable_plane		= drm_atomic_helper_disable_plane,
@@ -911,6 +969,27 @@ static int sun60i_kms_plane_init(struct sun60i_kms *kms,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int sun60i_kms_cursor_init(struct sun60i_kms *kms,
+				  struct drm_plane **out)
+{
+	struct sun60i_kms_plane *plane;
+
+	plane = drmm_universal_plane_alloc(kms->drm, struct sun60i_kms_plane,
+					   base, 0, &sun60i_kms_plane_funcs,
+					   sun60i_kms_cursor_formats,
+					   ARRAY_SIZE(sun60i_kms_cursor_formats),
+					   sun60i_kms_plane_modifiers,
+					   DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR, NULL);
+	if (IS_ERR(plane))
+		return PTR_ERR(plane);
+
+	plane->kms = kms;
+	drm_plane_helper_add(&plane->base, &sun60i_kms_cursor_helper_funcs);
+	*out = &plane->base;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 /*
  * The encoder, the bridge and the connector.
  *
@@ -978,6 +1057,13 @@ static int sun60i_kms_mode_config(struct sun60i_kms *kms)
 	drm->mode_config.min_height = 1;
 	drm->mode_config.max_width = SUN60I_KMS_MAX_FB_DIM;
 	drm->mode_config.max_height = SUN60I_KMS_MAX_FB_DIM;
+	/*
+	 * What DRM_CAP_CURSOR_WIDTH/HEIGHT report, and the buffer size a
+	 * compositor then allocates. A size hint, not a hardware bound: the
+	 * cursor layer takes any size the primary does.
+	 */
+	drm->mode_config.cursor_width = 64;
+	drm->mode_config.cursor_height = 64;
 	drm->mode_config.funcs = &sun60i_kms_mode_config_funcs;
 	drm->mode_config.helper_private = &sun60i_kms_mode_config_helpers;
 
@@ -1124,7 +1210,7 @@ static int sun60i_kms_attach_components(struct sun60i_kms *kms,
 static int sun60i_kms_bind(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct device_node *engine_np, *tcon_np;
-	struct drm_plane *primary;
+	struct drm_plane *primary, *cursor;
 	struct sun60i_kms *kms;
 	struct drm_device *drm;
 	int ret;
@@ -1178,7 +1264,11 @@ static int sun60i_kms_bind(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto unbind_all;
 
-	ret = drmm_crtc_init_with_planes(drm, &kms->crtc, primary, NULL,
+	ret = sun60i_kms_cursor_init(kms, &cursor);
+	if (ret)
+		goto unbind_all;
+
+	ret = drmm_crtc_init_with_planes(drm, &kms->crtc, primary, cursor,
 					 &sun60i_kms_crtc_funcs, NULL);
 	if (ret)
